# First Aid 1-300 for both factions: bandage recipes in orange/yellow order from
# professions.json, learned on as few trainer visits as the recipes allow. Expert
# is a book (Deneb Walker, Stromgarde / Balai Lok'Wein, Brackenwall Village);
# Artisan is the Triage quest, and the Triage doctor teaches Runecloth Bandage.
# Craft counts use the Classic skill-up chance (grey - skill) / (grey - yellow).
#
# Spawns, trainers and vendors come from the Era baseline (pfQuest); recipes and
# their skill colours from the Forever client tables (`profession build`).
# Nothing confirms the spawns' 10-60 placement on Forever yet: refine with
# Polestar_Recorder sessions. Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine
# converts them where Forever changed a map frame.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

step Learn First Aid
  tip Any First Aid trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice First Aid (character level 5); the arrow picks the nearest.
  level 5
  train First Aid Apprentice

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- First Aid 1-125

step Linen Bandage: cloth
  collect 2589 x61 nearest     -- humanoids of level 5-20 drop Linen Cloth (or buy it at the Auction House).

step Linen Bandage (1-50)
  tip Linen Bandage is orange from 1 (yellow at 30, grey at 60): about 61 crafts to 50. Bandages need no fire: craft them anywhere.
  craft 3275 until 50

step Journeyman First Aid
  tip Journeyman First Aid raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and character level 10: the arrow picks the nearest First Aid trainer of your faction. Learn Heavy Linen Bandage on the same visit.
  level 10
  train First Aid Journeyman
  learn 3276

